> - its limits: what it leaves to the caller, and what it never does.
{%- else %}
> - who it's for, and what it does for them, in their words rather than the code's;
> - how it differs from what they'd use instead, named, or by kind when you can't vouch for the
>   comparison;
{%- if primary == 'terminal' or primary == 'desktop' %}
> - whether it runs beside something else, such as a game or an editor;
{%- endif %}
> - its limits: what it doesn't do, and what it never sends, stores or shows.
{%- endif %}

